L["help.browse"] = "Browse on the left: pick Zone, Region (continent) or World. The button under them opens the zone picker: every zone with data, grouped by continent with counts and a filter box. Pick a zone to browse it from anywhere, a continent heading to browse the whole region, or Follow my position to track your current zone (/monstrator zone NAME and /monstrator region NAME work too). Then pick a list (Directory, Favorites, Review journal), an entry type and a category. Search matches NPC names, titles, IDs, zones, tags and service keywords."
L["help.subgroups"] = "Sub-groups: the > button beside a category narrows it further - Trainers by class or profession (Fishing, Blacksmithing...), Vendors by goods (Weapons, Food & drink, Reagents...) or profession supplies, Services (Bankers, Stable masters...), Transit, creatures by level or rank, and objects (Herbs, Mining nodes, Fishing pools...). Each sub-group shows how many results it has here; click the category itself to clear it. /monstrator find TEXT jumps straight there, e.g. /monstrator find fishing trainer or /monstrator find blacksmith."
L["help.results"] = "Results are sorted in the middle column; the coloured distance shows how far away each entry is. The Details column on the right follows your selection and offers Browse this zone (pins the entry's zone, or its continent if you are already there) plus a /way command for TomTom. Left-click or Enter navigates, right-click favorites. Map markers are not proof of an NPC spawn. Your scope, pinned zone and window position are remembered; /monstrator reset restores defaults."
L["help.database"] = "Monstrator ships its own Forever database: 10,000+ NPCs, 6,500+ objects (mailboxes, herbs, ore, chests, crafting stations), 14,000+ items and 4,000+ quests with spawn points. No other addon is required. Database records are not live-verified for this server; your confirmed observations always rank above them. /monstrator audit compares what you have seen in game with the database."
L["help.sort"] = "Sort cycles Nearest first (other zones grouped by region and zone), Zone A-Z (region > zone > distance), Name, Level and NPC ID. Evidence cycles the source filters. Pending observations always need review before becoming confirmed placements."
L["help.review"] = "Use Review to work through pending journal observations. Encounter positions are approximate; confirm a static placement only when you can verify it. NPC discovery is opt-in under Settings and records identities/encounters locally."
L["help.items"] = "Items (top right) opens the item lookup: search 14,000+ items by name or ID and see who sells, drops, gathers or rewards each one, nearest first. Left-click a source for a waypoint, right-click an NPC source for its 3D model, Show sources in directory lists every vendor and dropper in the main window. In Details, 3D model previews the selected NPC (uncached NPCs are requested from the server; items without a model show their icon) and Items sold/dropped lists that NPC's items."
L["help.scan"] = "NPC scan (footer button or /monstrator scan) alerts you with a sound, a raid-warning message and a popup when a watched NPC appears on a nameplate, as your target or mouseover, or as a minimap marker. Rare alerts also cover every rare and rare elite. Watch NPCs from Details (Watch for this NPC), by ID or exact name in the scan window, or with Watch target; names the database does not know are matched by name, which suits custom Forever NPCs. The popup offers Target (outside combat), Waypoint (where it was seen) and 3D model. Recent sightings are kept so you can head back later."
